 "status": "development, exploratory; not registered. E3 and E8 were each scored once against their own registrations; these readings are post hoc on delivered runs and inform the E7 registration",
 "definition": "E7 development (exploratory, not registered): the headroom race in the ViT, on the delivered E3 force exports\n(results/e3/forces.jsonl, epoch-20 counts in results/e3/runs.csv) and the E8 instrumented runs (raw runs from the\nrelease asset of results/e8/grid; final epoch-50 counts).\nThe decay part of the race is known exactly: weight decay is decoupled in code/vit_jepa.py (p <- p (1 - lr wd) per\nstep, SGD and AdamW alike), so a decayed linear output map loses 2 lr(t) wd(t) per step in log variance. The\nheadroom race reads the spectrum at a readout step t_r and lets every direction except the top lose that budget\nover the rest of the horizon, with no drive term after t_r and no fitted constant:\n    alive_k(T)  iff  log(e_k(t_r) / e_max(t_r)) - 2 sum_{t_r <= t < T} lr(t) wd(t)  >=  log 1e-3\n(the count rule of the measured counts; the top direction is held, as saturated by its drive). It is a race of\nlog headroom against the integrated decay; the drive enters only through the spectrum it has built by t_r.\nCompared with reading the count at t_r ('early') and, on E3, the registered step-0 horizon rule.\nArm-T weight-decay transition: lam_c(T) = the wd at which the seed-mean count crosses half the init count, by\nlog-linear interpolation along wd; predicted from the spectra of a low-decay reference row at t_r\n(count_pred(lam) = #{log(e_k/e_max) - 2 lr lam (T - t_r) >= log 1e-3}), at T = 20 and 50 epochs.",
